WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.816
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.816 --> 00:00:05.100
which takes about fifty
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.305
You'll place a connection
string in column A, B,

4
00:00:08.305 --> 00:00:12.175
C or D of the database axis,
and say who decides column D.

5
00:00:12.175 --> 00:00:17.004
You'll name the managed identity and
service-principal modes in each driver family,

6
00:00:17.004 --> 00:00:20.013
and say why the Entra password
mode is never a target.

7
00:00:20.013 --> 00:00:22.885
You'll run the kit's
connection scan over fixtures

8
00:00:22.885 --> 00:00:25.687
and read its masked strings,
columns and targets.

9
00:00:25.687 --> 00:00:29.388
And you'll list the three gates that
must hold before a string changes.

10
00:00:29.388 --> 00:00:32.504
Before you start, finish
Module 6, and Module 4,

11
00:00:32.504 --> 00:00:35.537
for the Entra login that
gate one checks for.

12
00:00:35.537 --> 00:00:40.990
The lab runs in PowerShell 7, in the kit
you unzipped into the F M W Labs folder.
